Planning and Development Office
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282
(Fax) 307-637-6366

MEMO
To:
Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council
From:
Charles W. Bloom, AICP, Planning and Development Director
Subject: A Resolution Approving the Jolly Rogers Urban Renewal Plan and Project Pursuant to
Wyoming Statute § 15-9-110.
Date:
June 10, 2024

Background:

The item for consideration is a Resolution.

The proposed Governing Body review schedule is as follows:
•
Introduction and Public Hearing
June 10, 2024
•
Public Services Committee

June 18, 2024
•
Final Consideration

June 24, 2024

Summary:

The City of Cheyenne adopted Ordinance No. 4381 and Resolution No. 6156 on June 28, 2021,
authorizing the creation and use of powers for the Urban Renewal Authority. Included within the Urban
Renewal Powers is the ability to make Urban Renewal Plans and Projects. The attached plan serves to
establish the Jolly Rogers Urban Renewal Plan and Project for the City of Cheyenne. The Governing Body
adopted a Resolution on July 10, 2023, declaring the area as blight pursuant to § 15-9-107, thus making
the area eligible for an Urban Renewal Plan and Project. The Jolly Rogers Urban Renewal Plan will
overview the urban renewal boundaries of the project area, the conditions of blight identified, all
authorized urban renewal activities, the project financing (including tax increment financing), the terms
of the plan, the conformance of the urban renewal project with adopted City of Cheyenne plans, the
conformance of the project with Wyo. Stat. § 15-9-110, and the procedures to amend the plan.

The Urban Renewal Authority Board considered the plan at their May 8, 2024, meeting and unanimously
recommended approval subject to staff’s recommendation. The item was then heard at the May 20,
2024, Planning Commission meeting and was unanimously approved by the Commission. The plan and
project reviewed by the Planning Commission reflected the conditions of URA approval.  The Planning
Commission staff report is attached and unchanged, except that the plan and project is attached to the
resolution instead of the staff report.

Attachments:
1. Resolution
2. Planning Commission Staff Report (Note, the Plan and Project has been omitted because it is
reincluded as Attachment A of the Resolution).

  Planning and Development Department
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282 (Fax) 307-637-6366
