Plan Financing
Stencil Group | AVI, PC.
Page 7
As mentioned in the previous section, the Jolly Roger Urban Renewal Plan and Project will utilize tax
increment financing. The base tax collected of the property included in the plan boundaries is $6,110.83.
Like other Urban Renewal Plans and Project in the City of Cheyenne each project will be required to
perform individually, meaning the project will only be able to collect TIF from the increment it creates. The
west lot will include the development of 194 apartment units comprised of studio, one-bedroom, and two-
bedroom units while the east lot’s development is yet to be determined. Each lot will be eligible to utilize
the increment that it produces individually; however, they may work together for the relocation of the water
and sewer lines. The TIF projections for the specified project will be provided once the Plan and Project
is approved. These projections will be based off of nearby apartment projects; such as Saddle Ridge and
Holmes corner.
Based on similar projects in the community, such as the Pointe Plaza, the increment is projected to be
approximately $250,000 per year.
